---
description: Perforce. Numbered CL, never submit.
globs: Source/**/*, Content/**/*, Config/**/*
alwaysApply: true
---

- NEVER suggest, generate, or execute a submit,
  commit, or `p4 submit`. The user validates the
  CL in Unreal before submitting.

# Start of work
- A new agent, or a feature to build, creates a
  numbered CL immediately. Short English
  description that names the feature. Default
  cannot hold a description.
- From the first edit, `p4 edit -c <CL>`,
  `p4 add -c <CL>`, or `p4 move -c <CL>`.
  Never leave that work on default.
- If the user names a CL, use that number.
- A new, moved, or renamed file on this work is
  `p4 add` or `p4 move` on that CL at once.
  Do not ask.

# One CL for files that depend on each other
- A change in A that only works with a change in
  B stays on the same numbered CL.
- If they must stay split because they are two
  features, stop and name the files, why they
  depend, and why they stay split. Do not move
  them without that warning.

# Description
- Keep it short and specific.
- Do not rewrite it after every edit.

# check CL
- When the user writes `check CL`, do not submit.
- Every file changed in this work is open on that
  numbered CL. Open or add a missing file that
  belongs there. Do not ask.
- Read the description and the diffs. Update it
  only if it no longer matches what was built
  (`p4 change -o <CL>`, then `p4 change -i`).
- Report the CL number, the files, and whether
  the description was left or corrected.
